al branch to the 'origin' remote (optionally injecting the token for auth).\", env_vars=[], args_schema=<class '__main__.GitPushInput'>, description_updated=False, cache_function=<function BaseTool.<lambda> at 0x7f068dfb4e00>, result_as_answer=False, max_usage_count=None, current_usage_count=0), FetchIssueTool(name='fetch_issue', description=\"Tool Name: fetch_issue\\nTool Arguments: {'owner': {'description': 'GitHub owner of the repository (DjoserKhemSimeu)', 'type': 'str'}, 'repo': {'description': 'Name of the GitHub repository(dummy_agent)', 'type': 'str'}, 'issue_number': {'description': 'Issue number (1)', 'type': 'Union[int, NoneType]'}}\\nTool Description: Fetches issues from the GitHub API. If the repository has only one issue, returns its JSON content 'body'.\", env_vars=[], args_schema=<class '__main__.FetchIssueInput'>, description_updated=False, cache_function=<function BaseTool.<lambda> at 0x7f068dfb4e00>, result_as_answer=False, max_usage_count=None, current_usage_count=0)]\n                \"agent_tools\": [name='git_clone' description=\"Tool Name: git_clone\\nTool Arguments: {'repo_url': {'description': 'SSH of the GitHub repository to clone', 'type': 'str'}}\\nTool Description: Clone a GitHub repository locally (uses the `git` CLI) and change into the cloned directory.\" env_vars=[] args_schema=<class '__main__.CloneRepoInput'> description_updated=False cache_function=<function BaseTool.<lambda> at 0x7f068dfb4e00> result_as_answer=False max_usage_count=None current_usage_count=0, name='git_create_branch' description=\"Tool Name: git_create_branch\\nTool Arguments: {'branch': {'description': 'Name of the branch to create', 'type': 'str'}, 'start_point': {'description': 'Start commit/branch (e.g., main)', 'type': 'Union[str, NoneType]'}, 'checkout': {'description': 'If True, switch to the new branch after creation', 'type': 'Union[bool, NoneType]'}}\\nTool Description: Create a new local branch and (optionally) checkout to it.\" env_vars=[] args_schem