put'> description_updated=False cache_function=<function BaseTool.<lambda> at 0x7f068dfb4e00> result_as_answer=False max_usage_count=None current_usage_count=0, name='git_push' description=\"Tool Name: git_push\\nTool Arguments: {'force': {'description': 'Push with --force if necessary', 'type': 'Union[bool, NoneType]'}}\\nTool Description: Pushes the local branch to the 'origin' remote (optionally injecting the token for auth).\" env_vars=[] args_schema=<class '__main__.GitPushInput'> description_updated=False cache_function=<function BaseTool.<lambda> at 0x7f068dfb4e00> result_as_answer=False max_usage_count=None current_usage_count=0, name='fetch_issue' description=\"Tool Name: fetch_issue\\nTool Arguments: {'owner': {'description': 'GitHub owner of the repository (DjoserKhemSimeu)', 'type': 'str'}, 'repo': {'description': 'Name of the GitHub repository(dummy_agent)', 'type': 'str'}, 'issue_number': {'description': 'Issue number (1)', 'type': 'Union[int, NoneType]'}}\\nTool Description: Fetches issues from the GitHub API. If the repository has only one issue, returns its JSON content 'body'.\" env_vars=[] args_schema=<class '__main__.FetchIssueInput'> description_updated=False cache_function=<function BaseTool.<lambda> at 0x7f068dfb4e00> result_as_answer=False max_usage_count=None current_usage_count=0] \n Create the most descriptive plan based on the tasks descriptions, tools available, and agents' goals for them to execute their goals with perfection.\n\nThis is the expected criteria for your final answer: Step by step plan on how the agents can execute their tasks using the available tools with mastery\nyou MUST return the actual complete content as the final answer, not a summary.\nEnsure your final answer strictly adheres to the following OpenAPI schema: {\n  \"description\": \"Output format for task planning results.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"list_of_plans_per_task\": {\n      \"description\": \"Step by step plan on how the agents can execute their tasks using the available tools with mastery\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"description\": \"Represents a plan for a specific task.\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"task\": {\n            \"description\": \"The task for which the plan is created\",\n            \"title\": \"Task\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"plan\": {\n            \"description\": \"The step by step plan on how the agents can execute their tasks using the available tools with mastery\",\n            \"title\": \"Plan\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"task\",\n          \"plan\"\n        ],\n        \"title\": \"PlanPerTask\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      },\n      \"title\": \"List Of Plans Per Task\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"list_of_plans_per_task\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"PlannerTaskPydanticOutput\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}\n\nDo not include the OpenAPI schema in the final output. Ensure the final output does not include any code block markers like ```json or ```python.\n\nBegin! This is VERY important to you, use the tools available and give your best Final Answer, your job depends on it!\n\nThought:\n\n<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\n```json\n{\n  \"list_of_plans_per_task\": [\n    {\n      \"task\": \"Fix the provided issue: clone the repo, diagnose, propose a patch, and create a PR if tests pass.\",\n      \"plan\": \"1. **Fetch Issue Details:** Use the `fetch_issue` tool to retrieve the details of issue number 1 from the `DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent` repository. This will provide context and the issue description.\\n2. **Clone Repository:** Use the `git_clone` tool to clone the `DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent` repository to a local directory. This will allow for local modifications and testing.\\n3. **Create a Branch:**  Use the `git_create_branch` tool to create a new branch, named something descriptive like `fix-issue-1`, based on the `main` branch.  This isolates the changes.\\n4. **Analyze the Issue:** Carefully read the issue description obtained in step 1. Examine the relevant code files to understand the root cause of the problem. Use the `read_file` tool if needed to inspect specific code sections.\\n5. **Propose a Patch:** Modify the code to address the identified issue.  Use the `write_file` tool to make the necessary changes. Ensure the solution is correct and doesn't introduce new problems.\\n6. **Run Tests:** Use the `run_tests` tool to execute the test suite and verify the fix.  Ensure all tests pass after the modification.\\n7. **Commit Changes:** If tests pass, use the `git_commit` tool to commit the changes to the local repository with a descriptive commit message.\\n8. **Push Branch:** Use the `git_push` tool to push the newly created branch to the `origin` remote repository. This makes the fix available for review.\\n9. **Report Actions:** Report the URL of the pushed branch to indicate the completion of the task and the location of the proposed fix.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```" ids="[105 2364 107 10354 1804 236787 107 3048 659 12883 62417 95947 236761 95947 8726 573 13919 6995 107 11069 3577 5671 563 236787 5180 5671 563 531 2619 614 8573 9813 236764 2918 236772 2003 236772 9340 2731 2721 580 506 9395 532 6436 2487 531 1546 8726 834 600 901 740 2121 506 9395 528 614 60823 8155 107 2021 2583 1041 1791 4133 1626 3890 531 506 4209 8932 1699 506 4453 2269 6518 236787 108 63254 236787 564 1492 740 2583 496 1822 3890 107 17667 25685 236787 5180 1626 3890 1921 577 506 1822 532 506 1346 4133 618 2653 236764 625 1921 577 14421 4970 236761 108 236777 59931 1161 1239 27857 236764 1041 3195 9796 580 625 236888 108 10354 7486 236787 108 8782 12883 236787 18186 580 1239 9395 12323 236787 236743 107 152 6804 9661 236743 236770 753 143280 236772 93868 24478 236787 36819 506 3847 4186 236787 30304 506 34691 236764 58355