time=2025-12-21T18:06:40.040+01:00 level=TRACE source=sentencepiece.go:188 msg=encoded string="<start_of_turn>user\n### System:\nYou are issue-fixer. ISSUE-FIXER:Autonomous agent to diagnose, propose, and apply fixes on GitHub repositories. (invoked by user 0)\nYour personal goal is: In the repository git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git, resolve the GitHub issue number 1 locally and propose PRs. Context: run by user_id=0. Local environment 'dummy_agent', owner='DjoserKhemSimeu', repo='dummy_agent'.$$$RUN_ID: USER_ID=0 NB_USER=1 MODEL=gemma3:12b ITER=0 HOST=http://127.0.0.1:53100$$$\nYou ONLY have access to the following tools, and should NEVER make up tools that are not listed here:\n\nTool Name: git_clone\nTool Arguments: {'repo_url': {'description': 'SSH of the GitHub repository to clone', 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Clone a GitHub repository locally (uses the `git` CLI) and change into the cloned directory.\nTool Name: git_create_branch\nTool Arguments: {'branch': {'description': 'Name of the branch to create', 'type': 'str'}, 'start_point': {'description': 'Start commit/branch (e.g., main)', 'type': 'Union[str, NoneType]'}, 'checkout': {'description': 'If True, switch to the new branch after creation', 'type': 'Union[bool, NoneType]'}}\nTool Description: Create a new local branch and (optionally) checkout to it.\nTool Name: read_file\nTool Arguments: {'path': {'description': \"Relative path in the repo to the file to read, if you already used git clone you don't need to put the name of the repo\", 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Reads a file in the cloned repository and returns its content.\nTool Name: write_file\nTool Arguments: {'path': {'description': 'Relative path in the repo to the file to write', 'type': 'str'}, 'content': {'description': 'Content to write', 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Writes content to a file in the cloned repository (creates directories if needed).\nTool Name: run_tests\nTool Arguments: {'pytest_args': {'description': 'Additional arguments for pytest', 'type': 'Union[str, NoneType]'}}\nTool Description: Runs the test suite via `pytest` if present in the repository.\nTool Name: git_commit\nTool Arguments: {'message': {'description': None, 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Stage and commit changes in the local repository.\nTool Name: git_push\nTool Arguments: {'force': {'description': 'Push with --force if necessary', 'type': 'Union[bool, NoneType]'}}\nTool Description: Pushes the local branch to the 'origin' remote (optionally injecting the token for auth).\nTool Name: fetch_issue\nTool Arguments: {'owner': {'description': 'GitHub owner of the repository (DjoserKhemSimeu)', 'type': 'str'}, 'repo': {'description': 'Name of the GitHub repository(dummy_agent)', 'type': 'str'}, 'issue_number': {'description': 'Issue number (1)', 'type': 'Union[int, NoneType]'}}\nTool Description: Fetches issues from the GitHub API. If the repository has only one issue, returns its JSON content 'body'.\n\nIMPORTANT: Use the following format in your response:\n\n```\nThought: you should always think about what to do\nAction: the action to take, only one name of [git_clone, git_create_branch, read_file, write_file, run_tests, git_commit, git_push, fetch_issue], just the name, exactly as it's written.\nAction Input: the input to the action, just a simple JSON object, enclosed in curly braces, using \" to wrap keys and values.\nObservation: the result of the action\n```\n\nOnce all necessary information is gathered, return the following format:\n\n```\nThought: I now know the final answer\nFinal Answer: the final answer to the original input question\n```\n\n### User:\n\nCurrent Task: TASK-PLANNER:Fix the provided issue: clone the repo, diagnose, propose a patch, and create a PR if tests pass. The update pipeline should be the following:1. Clone the GitHub repository locally an jump into it.2. Create a new branch for the changes.3. Analyze the issue and the code to identify the root of the issue.4. Make the necessary changes to the source code.5. Run the test suite to validate the changes.6. If tests pass, commit the changes and push the branch to the remote repository.$$$RUN_ID: USER_ID=0 NB_USER=1 MODEL=gemma3:12b ITER=0 HOST=http://127.0.0.1:53100$$$1. **Fetch Issue Details:** Use the `fetch_issue` tool to retrieve the details of issue number 1 from the `DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent` repository. This will provide context and the issue description.\n2. **Clone Repository:** Use the `git_clone` tool to clone the `DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent` repository to a local directory. This will allow for local modifications and testing.\n3. **Create a Branch:**  Use the `git_create_branch` tool to create a new branch, named something descriptive like `fix-issue-1`, based on the `main` branch.  This isolates the changes.\n4. **Analyze the Issue:** Carefully read the issue description obtained in step 1. Examine the relevant code files to understand the root cause of the problem. Use the `read_file` tool if needed to inspect specific code sections.\n5. **Propose a Patch:** Modify the code to address the identified issue.  Use the `write_file` tool to make the necessary changes. Ensure the solution is correct and doesn't introduce new problems.\n6. **Run Tests:** Use the `run_tests` tool to execute the test suite and verify the fix.  Ensure all tests pass after the modification.\n7. **Commit Changes:** If tests pass, use the `git_commit` tool to commit the changes to the local repository with a descriptive commit message.\n8. **Push Branch:** Use the `git_push` tool to push the newly created branch to the `origin` remote repository. This makes the fix available for review.\n9. **Report Actions:** Report the URL of the pushed branch to indicate the completion of the task and the location of the proposed fix.\n\nThis is the expected criteria for your final answer: Report of the actions taken, including the URL of the created branch pushed.\nyou MUST return the actual complete content as the final answer, not a summary.\n\nBegin! This is VERY important to you, use the tools available and give your best Final Answer, your job depends on it!\n\nThought:\n\n### Assistant:\n```\nThought: First, I need to fetch the details of issue number 1.\nAction: fetch_issue\nAction Input: {\"owner\": \"DjoserKhemSimeu\", \"repo\": \"dummy_agent\", \"issue_number\": 1}\nObservation: Bonjour,\n\nLorsque j'exécute `app.py`, une erreur apparaît :\n\n    NameError: name 'c' is not defined\n\nLa fonction `addition(a, b)` utilise `c` alors que cette variable n'existe pas.  \nLa ligne suivante pose problème :\n\n    return a + c\n\nSolution attendue : remplacer `c` par `b`.\n\nMerci !Thought: Now that I have the issue details, I should clone the repository.\nAction: git_clone\nAction Input: {\"repo_url\": \"git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git\"}\nObservation: Cloned to: dummy_agent and jumped into it\n\n<end_of_turn>\n<start_of_turn>model\nThought: Now I need to create a new branch for the changes.\nAction: git_create_branch\nAction Input: {\"branch\": \"fix-issue-1\", \"start_point\": \"main\", \"checkout\": true}" ids="[105 2364 107 10354 1804 236787 107 3048 659 4186 236772 9462 497 236761 170435 236772 51022 1089 236787 209380 8726 531 58355 236764 20017 236764 532 5510 49048 580 34115 82341 236761 568 18034 15320 684 2430 236743 236771 236768 107 11069 3577 5671 563 236787 799 506 20387 23032 236940 5846 236761 854 236787 236796 21434 497 236855 12427 236773 764 236756 236786 49152 236779 20154 236761 13705 236764 14245 506 34115 4186 1548 236743 236770 16445 532 20017 9206 236751 236761 17605 236787 1845 684 2430 236779 547 236784 236771 236761 12263 3453 756 49152 236779 20154 963 8123 2507 236796 21434 497 236855 12427 236773 764 236756 963 34691 2507 49152 236779 20154 6748 9873 236795 45562 236779 1735 236787 33181 236779 1735 236784 236771 55740 236779 20791 236784 236770 61507 236784 236759 12367 236800 236787 236770 236778 236763 2024