lete content as the final answer, not a summary.\n\nBegin! This is VERY important to you, use the tools available and give your best Final Answer, your job depends on it!\n\nThought:\n\n### Assistant:\n```\nThought: First, I need to fetch the details of issue number 1.\nAction: fetch_issue\nAction Input: {\"owner\": \"DjoserKhemSimeu\", \"repo\": \"dummy_agent\", \"issue_number\": 1}\nObservation: Bonjour,\n\nLorsque j'exécute `app.py`, une erreur apparaît :\n\n    NameError: name 'c' is not defined\n\nLa fonction `addition(a, b)` utilise `c` alors que cette variable n'existe pas.  \nLa ligne suivante pose problème :\n\n    return a + c\n\nSolution attendue : remplacer `c` par `b`.\n\nMerci !Thought: Now that I have the issue details, I should clone the repository.\nAction: git_clone\nAction Input: {\"repo_url\": \"git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git\"}\nObservation: Cloned to: dummy_agent and jumped into itThought: Now I need to create a new branch for the changes.\nAction: git_create_branch\nAction Input: {\"branch\": \"fix-issue-1\", \"start_point\": \"main\", \"checkout\": true}\nObservation: Branch 'fix-issue-1_0' created\n\n\nYou ONLY have access to the following tools, and should NEVER make up tools that are not listed here:\n\nTool Name: git_clone\nTool Arguments: {'repo_url': {'description': 'SSH of the GitHub repository to clone', 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Clone a GitHub repository locally (uses the `git` CLI) and change into the cloned directory.\nTool Name: git_create_branch\nTool Arguments: {'branch': {'description': 'Name of the branch to create', 'type': 'str'}, 'start_point': {'description': 'Start commit/branch (e.g., main)', 'type': 'Union[str, NoneType]'}, 'checkout': {'description': 'If True, switch to the new branch after creation', 'type': 'Union[bool, NoneType]'}}\nTool Description: Create a new local branch and (optionally) checkout to it.\nTool Name: read_file\nTool Arguments: {'path': {'description': \"Relative path in t